            <link>https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/ohio-becomes-midterm-battleground-after-years-of-republican-wins</link>
            <description><![CDATA[In recent presidential elections, Ohio has become a reliably Republican state. But in this year's midterms, it's once again a battleground. The races for governor and U.S. Senate are both seen as toss-ups by The Cook Political Report, and there are a handful of competitive House districts. Liz Landers reports on how national issues are affecting Ohio voters as they prepare to head to the polls.]]></description>
